"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Chinese Aircraft And Ships Detected: Taiwan tracks jets and PLAN vessels; warns of rising maritime pressure]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135649926.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Taiwan's Ministry of National Defence has observed a surge in Chinese military maneuvers surrounding the island, showcasing four separate sorties of aircraft and multiple naval vessels encroaching upon Taiwan's Air Defence Identification Zone. The Coast Guard has actively countered China's coast guard efforts, reaffirming Taiwan's sovereignty over its surrounding waters.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/taiwan-detects-4-chinese-military-aircraft-8-ships-around-island-in-24-hours/articleshow/135649926.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/taiwan-detects-4-chinese-military-aircraft-8-ships-around-island-in-24-hours/articleshow/135649926.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T08:35:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135649993,imgsize-78065.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Falling birth rates, fading faith? Pope Leo's message to Uruguay's youth]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135649712.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Pope Leo XIV urged young people in Uruguay to marry and start families as he continued his South American tour. He emphasized the importance of lifelong commitment and addressing declining birth rates in the country. The Pope also called on Uruguayans to strengthen their faith and build community bonds during his visit. Additionally, he visited neighborhoods affected by violence and highlighted the church's supportive initiatives.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/falling-birth-rates-fading-faith-pope-leos-message-to-uruguays-youth/articleshow/135649712.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/falling-birth-rates-fading-faith-pope-leos-message-to-uruguays-youth/articleshow/135649712.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T08:18:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135649831,imgsize-1064051.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Who is Qiulae Wong? New Zealand's potential kingmaker after cliffhanger election]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135649816.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Qiulae Wong, a 38-year-old politician who entered politics less than a year ago, could emerge as a kingmaker in New Zealand after the general election delivered no clear winner. Her centrist Opportunity Party is projected to win seven seats, potentially giving it a decisive role in government formation. Wong's party is pushing sweeping tax reforms, including a universal basic income funded by a land tax.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/who-is-qiulae-wong-new-zealands-potential-kingmaker-after-cliffhanger-election/articleshow/135649816.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/who-is-qiulae-wong-new-zealands-potential-kingmaker-after-cliffhanger-election/articleshow/135649816.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T08:08:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135649829,imgsize-1085761.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dozens Killed In Yemen Strikes: Saudi raids reportedly hit homes; UN truce collapse feared]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135649654.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[On Saturday, a series of Saudi airstrikes struck a village near Sanaa, resulting in a tragic loss of life and numerous injuries. This marks one of the worst incidents since the resumption of hostilities between the Saudi coalition and the Houthis. Among the casualties were many women and children, with some victims still trapped under rubble. This new wave of violence has effectively shattered a prior ceasefire in the area.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/at-least-33-killed-in-saudi-airstrikes-on-yemen-village-most-casualties-women-children/articleshow/135649654.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/at-least-33-killed-in-saudi-airstrikes-on-yemen-village-most-casualties-women-children/articleshow/135649654.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T07:48:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135649673,imgsize-120547.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Fresh Houthi threat? Saudi Arabia issues potential danger alerts in 3 cities]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135649607.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/saudi-arabia-issues-danger-alerts-for-dammam-dhahran-and-abqaiq-amid-houthi-threats/articleshow/135649607.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/saudi-arabia-issues-danger-alerts-for-dammam-dhahran-and-abqaiq-amid-houthi-threats/articleshow/135649607.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026